From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Miguel Fuertes <hkfuertes@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 09:16:39 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] android: cooperative pthread cancellation for bionic

Android lacks pthread_cancel. Provide a SIGUSR1 cooperative shim and add
explicit cancellation checks where glibc would have cancellation points:
the AP2 control/realtime receivers (poll, 250 ms ceiling), the event
receiver (accept and idle loop), and the buffered-audio processor and TCP
reader (condition waits, accept, recv). A cancel wake-up (EINTR) is tested
immediately. Before cancelling the event receiver, shutdown() its listening
socket so a blocked accept() returns at once instead of racing the signal.

Upstream: not submitted (Android/Bionic only; not needed with glibc/musl)
Signed-off-by: Miguel Fuertes <hkfuertes@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 ap2_buffered_audio_processor.c |  5 +++-
 ap2_event_receiver.c           |  1 +
 common.c                       | 45 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
